I've written the plan for two tasks, but the commit didn't happen: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused it. The files exist on disk at session_plan/task_01.md, task_02.md and issue_responses.md. The harness's own commit command ends in || true, so it would have failed the same way without stopping anything.

Task 1 (product, my own pick): two shell commands that report success when they failed.
• `yoyo ast`: exits 0 when ast-grep isn't installed, or (per an earlier probe) when the search errors. A script can't tell that apart from "searched, found nothing". It will copy the error and no-match exit codes yoyo grep already uses.
• `yoyo goal set` with no description: exits 0 after printing usage. It will exit 2 like the other usage errors. Bare, empty-string and whitespace-only input each get their own test row, and goal set "text" must still exit 0.

Nobody chooses to land in either branch, so there's no reason for exit 0. The REPL's wording stays the same. The real-binary test runs with a PATH pointing at an empty temp dir so it can't find ast-grep, and borrows an existing test file's key-scrubbing helper rather than starting a new one.

Task 2 (evolve, backlog drain): closes #1071. This is the open self-filed issue with the least work left. @yuanhao finished the protected workflow half. My half is adding "synthesize" to PHASE_SPEND_PHASES in scripts/extract_trajectory.py, and he asked me to confirm the stray test-model records are gone. I checked that while planning, on the audit-log branch:
• Before the fix (0a8b7113): the Day 240 row where the dreams step ran had four test-model records with no cost.
• After the fix: the 2026-10-28T18:09Z row, where dreams also ran, has three priced records ($1.09, $0.54, $0.83) and no test-model records.

extract_trajectory.py is not on evolve.sh's protected list, so the change can land.

Not taken this session: the remaining #1086 verbs that print /verb syntax on the shell (at least 12), and dotted model ids like claude-opus-5.5 silently getting an older preset. The dotted-id fix first needs a check of which ids Anthropic and the gateways actually accept, which doesn't fit a 30-minute task. No release, since none is due.
